    "result_text": "All changes are in place and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key per the specification.\n\n**New identity key** \u2014 `Owner.getIdentityKey()` (`model/Owner.java`) now returns the lower-case SHA-256 hex (64 chars) over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`, replacing the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` string. Telephone and email are already stored normalized (E.164 / lower-cased) by `ValidateOwnerFields`; the last name now contributes only through its Soundex code.\n\n**Soundex utility** \u2014 added `model/Soundex.java`, a standard American Soundex encoder (first letter + three consonant-group digits, with the h/w-transparent collapsing rule), used by both the identity key and the soft-match.\n\n**Hard-duplicate 409** \u2014 `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` already compared whole identity keys, so it now naturally keys on the new SHA-256 value. It still skips deleted owners, and the email-domain blocklist still runs earlier in validation. Because telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same last name/postcode but different telephones no longer collide, so the old household-id 409 path is gone. Docs/comments updated.\n\n**Soft-match** \u2014 `AssignPossibleDuplicate` now flags a possible duplicate when `soundex(lastName)` **and** `postcode` match an existing non-deleted owner but the `identityKey` differs (previously it compared last name case-insensitively and excluded same-telephone matches).\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated the `identityKey` schema description in `openapi.yml` and the comments in `owners.POST.yml` to describe the new key. `AssignHousehold`/`householdId` remain unchanged since they still feed household-size and membership-cap logic; only duplicate detection moved to the single identity key.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` asserting the 64-hex shape, and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` asserting a 409 on identical identity) both pass, along with the rest of the suite.",
